items.a:
enum Discount {
    STUDENT(0.20),  // 20% discount → 800.0
    SENIOR(0.30);   // 30% discount → 700.0
    private final double rate;
    Discount(double rate) { this.rate = rate; } // private constructor
    public double apply(double price) { return price * (1 - rate); }
}
Output:
800.0
700.0
Key points filled in: (1) Constructor arguments in constant declaration (0.20, 0.30). (2) Constructor name matches enum name — Discount(double rate). (3) Uses this.rate in apply(). The constructor is implicitly private.
